# Trivy Ignore File
# This file contains CVEs that are known and accepted for specific reasons
# Document each ignored CVE with a clear explanation

# =============================================================================
# Base Image Vulnerabilities (Microsoft .NET Runtime)
# =============================================================================
# These are vulnerabilities in the base Microsoft .NET runtime images
# that we cannot directly fix. They require Microsoft to update the base image.
# We monitor these and update our base images when patches are available.

# Example format (uncomment and add actual CVEs as needed):
# CVE-2024-XXXXX  # .NET runtime vulnerability - waiting for Microsoft patch
# CVE-2024-YYYYY  # Alpine Linux base image - no fix available yet

# =============================================================================
# Base Image Vulnerabilities (Alpine Linux)
# =============================================================================
# The nginx:alpine image may contain base OS vulnerabilities
# that are pending upstream fixes.

# Example:
# CVE-2024-XXXXX  # Alpine APK package - no fix available

# =============================================================================
# INSTRUCTIONS
# =============================================================================
# To ignore a CVE:
# 1. Research the CVE to understand the risk
# 2. Document why it's being ignored (no fix available, false positive, etc.)
# 3. Add the CVE ID as a new line in this file
# 4. Set a reminder to re-evaluate periodically
# 5. Consider if there are mitigating controls in place

# =============================================================================
# POLICY
# =============================================================================
# - Only ignore CVEs after thorough review and documentation
# - Prefer fixing over ignoring whenever possible
# - Re-evaluate ignored CVEs monthly
# - Never ignore application-level vulnerabilities
# - Team lead approval required for ignoring CRITICAL severity CVEs
